From bbe4f76f4efe712d6ad22680783e947f7ef9aac1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caoanhhao <caoanhhao@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:17:23 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] misc: goodix_fp_tz: power, clocks and interrupt of a
 TrustZone-driven sensor

Samsung's goodix_fp driver in TrustZone mode ("tz: 1") does no SPI: the
fingerprint trusted app reads the sensor, Linux switches the LDO and
reset, keeps the system awake while the app uses the bus and forwards
the sensor's interrupt. Add that as /dev/goodix_fp with the same ioctl
numbers as Samsung's driver (reset, enable/disable irq, spi clock,
power, orientation); read()/poll() wait for the interrupt and return
the interrupt count. The SPI clock ioctls also vote the serial engine
and QUP wrapper clocks and the QUP interconnect paths given in the DT.

caoanhhao used AI to code
